 like them but overall I  don't know how appealing it is to the  majority of our audience that doesn't  mean we can't do it we could do segments  that appeal to you know a niche of the  audience that's  Science and Technology doing something  science and technology related every  week in place of audience questions  that's a possibility but these are only  like three ideas so what I'm asking you  to think about and get in touch with me  david at david pakman.com if you have  strong feelings what else might you like  to see taking the place of audience  questions the top suggestions that we  get we will turn into a poll open it up  to the entire audience and then you will  ultimately decide what's going to  replace audience questions get in touch  I'm open to all ideas there's no such  thing as a bad idea there are ideas that  the audience might not enjoy and might  not be feasible for us to produce but I  want to hear anything that comes to mind  what segments is missing from the David  Pakman show that you would like to see  added because this is one of those  opportunities where we change the format  of the show and I want to hear from you  david at david pakman.com what should we  replace audience questions with
 

